      "## list\n\n`client.beta.assistants.list(after?: string, before?: string, limit?: number, order?: 'asc' | 'desc'): { id: string; created_at: number; description: string; instructions: string; metadata: metadata; model: string; name: string; object: 'assistant'; tools: assistant_tool[]; response_format?: assistant_response_format_option; temperature?: number; tool_resources?: object; top_p?: number; }`\n\n**get** `/assistants`\n\nReturns a list of assistants.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `after?: string`\n  A cursor for use in pagination. `after` is an object ID that defines your place in the list. For instance, if you make a list request and receive 100 objects, ending with obj_foo, your subsequent call can include after=obj_foo in order to fetch the next page of the list.\n\n\n- `before?: string`\n  A cursor for use in pagination. `before` is an object ID that defines your place in the list. For instance, if you make a list request and receive 100 objects, starting with obj_foo, your subsequent call can include before=obj_foo in order to fetch the previous page of the list.\n\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  A limit on the number of objects to be returned. Limit can range between 1 and 100, and the default is 20.\n\n\n- `order?: 'asc' | 'desc'`\n  Sort order by the `created_at` timestamp of the objects. `asc` for ascending order and `desc` for descending order.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; created_at: number; description: string; instructions: string; metadata: object; model: string; name: string; object: 'assistant'; tools: object | object | object[]; response_format?: 'auto' | object | object | object; temperature?: number; tool_resources?: { code_interpreter?: { file_ids?: string[]; }; file_search?: { vector_store_ids?: string[]; }; }; top_p?: number; }`\n  Represents an `assistant` that can call the model and use tools.\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `created_at: number`\n  - `description: string`\n  - `instructions: string`\n  - `metadata: object`\n  - `model: string`\n  - `name: string`\n  - `object: 'assistant'`\n  - `tools: { type: 'code_interpreter'; } | { type: 'file_search'; file_search?: { max_num_results?: number; ranking_options?: object; }; } | { function: object; type: 'function'; }[]`\n  - `response_format?: 'auto' | { type: 'text'; } | { type: 'json_object'; } | { json_schema: { name: string; description?: string; schema?: object; strict?: boolean; }; type: 'json_schema'; }`\n  - `temperature?: number`\n  - `tool_resources?: { code_interpreter?: { file_ids?: string[]; }; file_search?: { vector_store_ids?: string[]; }; }`\n  - `top_p?: number`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport OpenAI from 'openai-mcp-test';\n\nconst client = new OpenAI();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const assistant of client.beta.assistants.list()) {\n  console.log(assistant);\n}\n```",
