    markdown:
      "## update\n\n`client.beta.threads.update(thread_id: string, metadata?: object, tool_resources?: { code_interpreter?: { file_ids?: string[]; }; file_search?: { vector_store_ids?: string[]; }; }): { id: string; created_at: number; metadata: metadata; object: 'thread'; tool_resources: object; }`\n\n**post** `/threads/{thread_id}`\n\nModifies a thread.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `thread_id: string`\n\n- `metadata?: object`\n  Set of 16 key-value pairs that can be attached to an object. This can be\nuseful for storing additional information about the object in a structured\nformat, and querying for objects via API or the dashboard.\n\nKeys are strings with a maximum length of 64 characters. Values are strings\nwith a maximum length of 512 characters.\n\n\n- `tool_resources?: { code_interpreter?: { file_ids?: string[]; }; file_search?: { vector_store_ids?: string[]; }; }`\n  A set of resources that are made available to the assistant's tools in this thread. The resources are specific to the type of tool. For example, the `code_interpreter` tool requires a list of file IDs, while the `file_search` tool requires a list of vector store IDs.\n\n  - `code_interpreter?: { file_ids?: string[]; }`\n  - `file_search?: { vector_store_ids?: string[]; }`\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; created_at: number; metadata: object; object: 'thread'; tool_resources: { code_interpreter?: { file_ids?: string[]; }; file_search?: { vector_store_ids?: string[]; }; }; }`\n  Represents a thread that contains [messages](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/messages).\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `created_at: number`\n  - `metadata: object`\n  - `object: 'thread'`\n  - `tool_resources: { code_interpreter?: { file_ids?: string[]; }; file_search?: { vector_store_ids?: string[]; }; }`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport OpenAI from 'openai-mcp-test';\n\nconst client = new OpenAI();\n\nconst thread = await client.beta.threads.update('thread_id');\n\nconsole.log(thread);\n```",
