    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.beta.threads.runs.list(thread_id: string, after?: string, before?: string, limit?: number, order?: 'asc' | 'desc'): { id: string; assistant_id: string; cancelled_at: number; completed_at: number; created_at: number; expires_at: number; failed_at: number; incomplete_details: object; instructions: string; last_error: object; max_completion_tokens: number; max_prompt_tokens: number; metadata: metadata; model: string; object: 'thread.run'; parallel_tool_calls: boolean; required_action: object; response_format: assistant_response_format_option; started_at: number; status: run_status; thread_id: string; tool_choice: assistant_tool_choice_option; tools: assistant_tool[]; truncation_strategy: object; usage: object; temperature?: number; top_p?: number; }`\n\n**get** `/threads/{thread_id}/runs`\n\nReturns a list of runs belonging to a thread.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `thread_id: string`\n\n- `after?: string`\n  A cursor for use in pagination. `after` is an object ID that defines your place in the list. For instance, if you make a list request and receive 100 objects, ending with obj_foo, your subsequent call can include after=obj_foo in order to fetch the next page of the list.\n\n\n- `before?: string`\n  A cursor for use in pagination. `before` is an object ID that defines your place in the list. For instance, if you make a list request and receive 100 objects, starting with obj_foo, your subsequent call can include before=obj_foo in order to fetch the previous page of the list.\n\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  A limit on the number of objects to be returned. Limit can range between 1 and 100, and the default is 20.\n\n\n- `order?: 'asc' | 'desc'`\n  Sort order by the `created_at` timestamp of the objects. `asc` for ascending order and `desc` for descending order.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; assistant_id: string; cancelled_at: number; completed_at: number; created_at: number; expires_at: number; failed_at: number; incomplete_details: { reason?: 'max_completion_tokens' | 'max_prompt_tokens'; }; instructions: string; last_error: { code: 'server_error' | 'rate_limit_exceeded' | 'invalid_prompt'; message: string; }; max_completion_tokens: number; max_prompt_tokens: number; metadata: object; model: string; object: 'thread.run'; parallel_tool_calls: boolean; required_action: { submit_tool_outputs: { tool_calls: required_action_function_tool_call[]; }; type: 'submit_tool_outputs'; }; response_format: 'auto' | object | object | object; started_at: number; status: string; thread_id: string; tool_choice: 'none' | 'auto' | 'required' | object; tools: object | object | object[]; truncation_strategy: { type: 'auto' | 'last_messages'; last_messages?: number; }; usage: { completion_tokens: number; prompt_tokens: number; total_tokens: number; }; temperature?: number; top_p?: number; }`\n  Represents an execution run on a [thread](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/threads).\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `assistant_id: string`\n  - `cancelled_at: number`\n  - `completed_at: number`\n  - `created_at: number`\n  - `expires_at: number`\n  - `failed_at: number`\n  - `incomplete_details: { reason?: 'max_completion_tokens' | 'max_prompt_tokens'; }`\n  - `instructions: string`\n  - `last_error: { code: 'server_error' | 'rate_limit_exceeded' | 'invalid_prompt'; message: string; }`\n  - `max_completion_tokens: number`\n  - `max_prompt_tokens: number`\n  - `metadata: object`\n  - `model: string`\n  - `object: 'thread.run'`\n  - `parallel_tool_calls: boolean`\n  - `required_action: { submit_tool_outputs: { tool_calls: { id: string; function: object; type: 'function'; }[]; }; type: 'submit_tool_outputs'; }`\n  - `response_format: 'auto' | { type: 'text'; } | { type: 'json_object'; } | { json_schema: { name: string; description?: string; schema?: object; strict?: boolean; }; type: 'json_schema'; }`\n  - `started_at: number`\n  - `status: string`\n  - `thread_id: string`\n  - `tool_choice: 'none' | 'auto' | 'required' | { type: 'function' | 'code_interpreter' | 'file_search'; function?: object; }`\n  - `tools: { type: 'code_interpreter'; } | { type: 'file_search'; file_search?: { max_num_results?: number; ranking_options?: object; }; } | { function: object; type: 'function'; }[]`\n  - `truncation_strategy: { type: 'auto' | 'last_messages'; last_messages?: number; }`\n  - `usage: { completion_tokens: number; prompt_tokens: number; total_tokens: number; }`\n  - `temperature?: number`\n  - `top_p?: number`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport OpenAI from 'openai-mcp-test';\n\nconst client = new OpenAI();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const run of client.beta.threads.runs.list('thread_id')) {\n  console.log(run);\n}\n```",
