    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.beta.threads.messages.create(thread_id: string, content: string | object | object | object[], role: 'user' | 'assistant', attachments?: { file_id?: string; tools?: object | { type: 'file_search'; }[]; }[], metadata?: object): { id: string; assistant_id: string; attachments: object[]; completed_at: number; content: message_content[]; created_at: number; incomplete_at: number; incomplete_details: object; metadata: metadata; object: 'thread.message'; role: 'user' | 'assistant'; run_id: string; status: 'in_progress' | 'incomplete' | 'completed'; thread_id: string; }`\n\n**post** `/threads/{thread_id}/messages`\n\nCreate a message.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `thread_id: string`\n\n- `content: string | { image_file: object; type: 'image_file'; } | { image_url: object; type: 'image_url'; } | { text: string; type: 'text'; }[]`\n  The text contents of the message.\n\n- `role: 'user' | 'assistant'`\n  The role of the entity that is creating the message. Allowed values include:\n- `user`: Indicates the message is sent by an actual user and should be used in most cases to represent user-generated messages.\n- `assistant`: Indicates the message is generated by the assistant. Use this value to insert messages from the assistant into the conversation.\n\n- `attachments?: { file_id?: string; tools?: { type: 'code_interpreter'; } | { type: 'file_search'; }[]; }[]`\n  A list of files attached to the message, and the tools they should be added to.\n\n- `metadata?: object`\n  Set of 16 key-value pairs that can be attached to an object. This can be\nuseful for storing additional information about the object in a structured\nformat, and querying for objects via API or the dashboard.\n\nKeys are strings with a maximum length of 64 characters. Values are strings\nwith a maximum length of 512 characters.\n\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; assistant_id: string; attachments: { file_id?: string; tools?: object | { type: 'file_search'; }[]; }[]; completed_at: number; content: object | object | object | object[]; created_at: number; incomplete_at: number; incomplete_details: { reason: 'content_filter' | 'max_tokens' | 'run_cancelled' | 'run_expired' | 'run_failed'; }; metadata: object; object: 'thread.message'; role: 'user' | 'assistant'; run_id: string; status: 'in_progress' | 'incomplete' | 'completed'; thread_id: string; }`\n  Represents a message within a [thread](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/threads).\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `assistant_id: string`\n  - `attachments: { file_id?: string; tools?: { type: 'code_interpreter'; } | { type: 'file_search'; }[]; }[]`\n  - `completed_at: number`\n  - `content: { image_file: object; type: 'image_file'; } | { image_url: object; type: 'image_url'; } | { text: object; type: 'text'; } | { refusal: string; type: 'refusal'; }[]`\n  - `created_at: number`\n  - `incomplete_at: number`\n  - `incomplete_details: { reason: 'content_filter' | 'max_tokens' | 'run_cancelled' | 'run_expired' | 'run_failed'; }`\n  - `metadata: object`\n  - `object: 'thread.message'`\n  - `role: 'user' | 'assistant'`\n  - `run_id: string`\n  - `status: 'in_progress' | 'incomplete' | 'completed'`\n  - `thread_id: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport OpenAI from 'openai-mcp-test';\n\nconst client = new OpenAI();\n\nconst message = await client.beta.threads.messages.create('thread_id', { content: 'string', role: 'user' });\n\nconsole.log(message);\n```",
