    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.beta.threads.messages.list(thread_id: string, after?: string, before?: string, limit?: number, order?: 'asc' | 'desc', run_id?: string): { id: string; assistant_id: string; attachments: object[]; completed_at: number; content: message_content[]; created_at: number; incomplete_at: number; incomplete_details: object; metadata: metadata; object: 'thread.message'; role: 'user' | 'assistant'; run_id: string; status: 'in_progress' | 'incomplete' | 'completed'; thread_id: string; }`\n\n**get** `/threads/{thread_id}/messages`\n\nReturns a list of messages for a given thread.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `thread_id: string`\n\n- `after?: string`\n  A cursor for use in pagination. `after` is an object ID that defines your place in the list. For instance, if you make a list request and receive 100 objects, ending with obj_foo, your subsequent call can include after=obj_foo in order to fetch the next page of the list.\n\n\n- `before?: string`\n  A cursor for use in pagination. `before` is an object ID that defines your place in the list. For instance, if you make a list request and receive 100 objects, starting with obj_foo, your subsequent call can include before=obj_foo in order to fetch the previous page of the list.\n\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  A limit on the number of objects to be returned. Limit can range between 1 and 100, and the default is 20.\n\n\n- `order?: 'asc' | 'desc'`\n  Sort order by the `created_at` timestamp of the objects. `asc` for ascending order and `desc` for descending order.\n\n- `run_id?: string`\n  Filter messages by the run ID that generated them.\n\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; assistant_id: string; attachments: { file_id?: string; tools?: object | { type: 'file_search'; }[]; }[]; completed_at: number; content: object | object | object | object[]; created_at: number; incomplete_at: number; incomplete_details: { reason: 'content_filter' | 'max_tokens' | 'run_cancelled' | 'run_expired' | 'run_failed'; }; metadata: object; object: 'thread.message'; role: 'user' | 'assistant'; run_id: string; status: 'in_progress' | 'incomplete' | 'completed'; thread_id: string; }`\n  Represents a message within a [thread](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/threads).\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `assistant_id: string`\n  - `attachments: { file_id?: string; tools?: { type: 'code_interpreter'; } | { type: 'file_search'; }[]; }[]`\n  - `completed_at: number`\n  - `content: { image_file: object; type: 'image_file'; } | { image_url: object; type: 'image_url'; } | { text: object; type: 'text'; } | { refusal: string; type: 'refusal'; }[]`\n  - `created_at: number`\n  - `incomplete_at: number`\n  - `incomplete_details: { reason: 'content_filter' | 'max_tokens' | 'run_cancelled' | 'run_expired' | 'run_failed'; }`\n  - `metadata: object`\n  - `object: 'thread.message'`\n  - `role: 'user' | 'assistant'`\n  - `run_id: string`\n  - `status: 'in_progress' | 'incomplete' | 'completed'`\n  - `thread_id: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport OpenAI from 'openai-mcp-test';\n\nconst client = new OpenAI();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const message of client.beta.threads.messages.list('thread_id')) {\n  console.log(message);\n}\n```",
