    params: ['after?: string;', 'limit?: number;'],
    response:
      "{ id: string; completion_window: string; created_at: number; endpoint: string; input_file_id: string; object: 'batch'; status: string; cancelled_at?: number; cancelling_at?: number; completed_at?: number; error_file_id?: string; errors?: { data?: object[]; object?: string; }; expired_at?: number; expires_at?: number; failed_at?: number; finalizing_at?: number; in_progress_at?: number; metadata?: object; model?: string; output_file_id?: string; request_counts?: { completed: number; failed: number; total: number; }; usage?: { input_tokens: number; input_tokens_details: object; output_tokens: number; output_tokens_details: object; total_tokens: number; }; }",
    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.batches.list(after?: string, limit?: number): { id: string; completion_window: string; created_at: number; endpoint: string; input_file_id: string; object: 'batch'; status: string; cancelled_at?: number; cancelling_at?: number; completed_at?: number; error_file_id?: string; errors?: object; expired_at?: number; expires_at?: number; failed_at?: number; finalizing_at?: number; in_progress_at?: number; metadata?: metadata; model?: string; output_file_id?: string; request_counts?: batch_request_counts; usage?: batch_usage; }`\n\n**get** `/batches`\n\nList your organization's batches.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `after?: string`\n  A cursor for use in pagination. `after` is an object ID that defines your place in the list. For instance, if you make a list request and receive 100 objects, ending with obj_foo, your subsequent call can include after=obj_foo in order to fetch the next page of the list.\n\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  A limit on the number of objects to be returned. Limit can range between 1 and 100, and the default is 20.\n\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; completion_window: string; created_at: number; endpoint: string; input_file_id: string; object: 'batch'; status: string; cancelled_at?: number; cancelling_at?: number; completed_at?: number; error_file_id?: string; errors?: { data?: object[]; object?: string; }; expired_at?: number; expires_at?: number; failed_at?: number; finalizing_at?: number; in_progress_at?: number; metadata?: object; model?: string; output_file_id?: string; request_counts?: { completed: number; failed: number; total: number; }; usage?: { input_tokens: number; input_tokens_details: object; output_tokens: number; output_tokens_details: object; total_tokens: number; }; }`\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `completion_window: string`\n  - `created_at: number`\n  - `endpoint: string`\n  - `input_file_id: string`\n  - `object: 'batch'`\n  - `status: string`\n  - `cancelled_at?: number`\n  - `cancelling_at?: number`\n  - `completed_at?: number`\n  - `error_file_id?: string`\n  - `errors?: { data?: { code?: string; line?: number; message?: string; param?: string; }[]; object?: string; }`\n  - `expired_at?: number`\n  - `expires_at?: number`\n  - `failed_at?: number`\n  - `finalizing_at?: number`\n  - `in_progress_at?: number`\n  - `metadata?: object`\n  - `model?: string`\n  - `output_file_id?: string`\n  - `request_counts?: { completed: number; failed: number; total: number; }`\n  - `usage?: { input_tokens: number; input_tokens_details: { cached_tokens: number; }; output_tokens: number; output_tokens_details: { reasoning_tokens: number; }; total_tokens: number; }`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport OpenAI from 'openai-mcp-test';\n\nconst client = new OpenAI();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const batch of client.batches.list()) {\n  console.log(batch);\n}\n```",
