    stainlessPath: '(resource) batches > (method) cancel',
    qualified: 'client.batches.cancel',
    params: ['batch_id: string;'],
    response:
      "{ id: string; completion_window: string; created_at: number; endpoint: string; input_file_id: string; object: 'batch'; status: string; cancelled_at?: number; cancelling_at?: number; completed_at?: number; error_file_id?: string; errors?: { data?: object[]; object?: string; }; expired_at?: number; expires_at?: number; failed_at?: number; finalizing_at?: number; in_progress_at?: number; metadata?: object; model?: string; output_file_id?: string; request_counts?: { completed: number; failed: number; total: number; }; usage?: { input_tokens: number; input_tokens_details: object; output_tokens: number; output_tokens_details: object; total_tokens: number; }; }",
    markdown:
      "## cancel\n\n`client.batches.cancel(batch_id: string): { id: string; completion_window: string; created_at: number; endpoint: string; input_file_id: string; object: 'batch'; status: string; cancelled_at?: number; cancelling_at?: number; completed_at?: number; error_file_id?: string; errors?: object; expired_at?: number; expires_at?: number; failed_at?: number; finalizing_at?: number; in_progress_at?: number; metadata?: metadata; model?: string; output_file_id?: string; request_counts?: batch_request_counts; usage?: batch_usage; }`\n\n**post** `/batches/{batch_id}/cancel`\n\nCancels an in-progress batch. The batch will be in status `cancelling` for up to 10 minutes, before changing to `cancelled`, where it will have partial results (if any) available in the output file.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `batch_id: string`\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; completion_window: string; created_at: number; endpoint: string; input_file_id: string; object: 'batch'; status: string; cancelled_at?: number; cancelling_at?: number; completed_at?: number; error_file_id?: string; errors?: { data?: object[]; object?: string; }; expired_at?: number; expires_at?: number; failed_at?: number; finalizing_at?: number; in_progress_at?: number; metadata?: object; model?: string; output_file_id?: string; request_counts?: { completed: number; failed: number; total: number; }; usage?: { input_tokens: number; input_tokens_details: object; output_tokens: number; output_tokens_details: object; total_tokens: number; }; }`\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `completion_window: string`\n  - `created_at: number`\n  - `endpoint: string`\n  - `input_file_id: string`\n  - `object: 'batch'`\n  - `status: string`\n  - `cancelled_at?: number`\n  - `cancelling_at?: number`\n  - `completed_at?: number`\n  - `error_file_id?: string`\n  - `errors?: { data?: { code?: string; line?: number; message?: string; param?: string; }[]; object?: string; }`\n  - `expired_at?: number`\n  - `expires_at?: number`\n  - `failed_at?: number`\n  - `finalizing_at?: number`\n  - `in_progress_at?: number`\n  - `metadata?: object`\n  - `model?: string`\n  - `output_file_id?: string`\n  - `request_counts?: { completed: number; failed: number; total: number; }`\n  - `usage?: { input_tokens: number; input_tokens_details: { cached_tokens: number; }; output_tokens: number; output_tokens_details: { reasoning_tokens: number; }; total_tokens: number; }`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport OpenAI from 'openai-mcp-test';\n\nconst client = new OpenAI();\n\nconst batch = await client.batches.cancel('batch_id');\n\nconsole.log(batch);\n```",
