    params: ['upload_id: string;', 'data: string;'],
    response: "{ id: string; created_at: number; object: 'upload.part'; upload_id: string; }",
    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.uploads.parts.create(upload_id: string, data: string): { id: string; created_at: number; object: 'upload.part'; upload_id: string; }`\n\n**post** `/uploads/{upload_id}/parts`\n\nAdds a [Part](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/uploads/part-object) to an [Upload](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/uploads/object) object. A Part represents a chunk of bytes from the file you are trying to upload. \n\nEach Part can be at most 64 MB, and you can add Parts until you hit the Upload maximum of 8 GB.\n\nIt is possible to add multiple Parts in parallel. You can decide the intended order of the Parts when you [complete the Upload](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/uploads/complete).\n\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `upload_id: string`\n\n- `data: string`\n  The chunk of bytes for this Part.\n\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; created_at: number; object: 'upload.part'; upload_id: string; }`\n  The upload Part represents a chunk of bytes we can add to an Upload object.\n\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `created_at: number`\n  - `object: 'upload.part'`\n  - `upload_id: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport OpenAI from 'openai-mcp-test';\n\nconst client = new OpenAI();\n\nconst uploadPart = await client.uploads.parts.create('upload_abc123', { data: fs.createReadStream('path/to/file') });\n\nconsole.log(uploadPart);\n```",
